# Problem record

A problem, from any source, under one identity, as the wire carries it. The JSON
is derived from this block (`toJson_Problem`, `fromJson_Problem`), so the wire is
a contract nobody writes a serializer for.

`id` names the problem across the factory: `opdp:116` for atlas record 116,
`op:OP001` for formalization-lab statement OP001, `fc:ErdosProblems/10` for a
formal-conjectures file. `cohort`, `collection` and `category` place it in the
atlas graph. The Lean fields are `none` for an informal problem, never an empty
text pretending to be a statement. `externalKey` is the source's own identity and
`crossRef` a source-independent handle (`erdos:10`) the link stage joins on.

## A Problem has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a title, which is Text.
    a source, which is Text.
    a cohort, which is Text.
    a collection, which is Text.
    a category, which is Text.
    a statementInformal, which is Text.
    a leanStatement, which is Option of Text.
    a leanModule, which is Option of Text.
    a leanDeclaration, which is Option of Text.
    an externalKey, which is Option of Text.
    a crossRef, which is Option of Text.
    a status, which is Text.

## Note
A problem's status as the coordinator records it, whatever words its source
uses: open, `solved_upstream`, `ill_posed`, `disputed`, or `unknown` — never a guess.

## To problemStatus (sourceStatus: Text) -> Text:
    If ["open", "source-reported-open", "partially_solved", "source_claimed_open", "status_unclear"] contains sourceStatus:
        Return "open".
    If sourceStatus is equal to "solved":
        Return "solved_upstream".
    If sourceStatus is equal to "ill_posed" or sourceStatus is equal to "disputed":
        Return sourceStatus.
    Return "unknown".

## Note
A problem with only an identity and a title, for sources that know no more.

## To bareProblem (id: Text, title: Text, source: Text) -> Problem:
    Let mutable p be a new Problem with id id and title title and source source and cohort source and collection source and category "miscellaneous".
    Set p's statementInformal to "".
    Set p's leanStatement to none.
    Set p's leanModule to none.
    Set p's leanDeclaration to none.
    Set p's externalKey to none.
    Set p's crossRef to none.
    Set p's status to "open".
    Return p.

## Note
A formalization-lab problem with every field filled, for the tests.

## To sampleProblem () -> Problem:
    Let mutable p be bareProblem("op:OP022", "ErdosProblems / 10", "formalization-lab").
    Set p's cohort to "formalization-lab-200".
    Set p's collection to "ErdosProblems".
    Set p's category to "number-theory".
    Set p's leanStatement to some "theorem erdos_10 : True".
    Set p's leanModule to some "FormalConjectures.ErdosProblems.«10»".
    Set p's leanDeclaration to some "Erdos10.erdos_10".
    Set p's externalKey to some "fc:ErdosProblems/10".
    Set p's crossRef to some "erdos:10".
    Return p.

## Test: a problem round-trips through its derived codec

Let p be sampleProblem().
Expect that fromJson_Problem(toJson_Problem(p)) is equal to a new Ok with value p.

## Test: an absent Lean statement travels as null, not as an empty text

Let p be bareProblem("opdp:116", "Gowers Box Norms", "opdp").
Expect that toJson_Problem(p) contains "\"leanStatement\":null".
Expect that fromJson_Problem(toJson_Problem(p)) is equal to a new Ok with value p.

## Test: source statuses map onto the coordinator's five

For each of these cases:

| source                 | status            |
|------------------------|-------------------|
| "source-reported-open" | "open"            |
| "partially_solved"     | "open"            |
| "solved"               | "solved_upstream" |
| "ill_posed"            | "ill_posed"       |
| "whatever"             | "unknown"         |

Expect that problemStatus(source) is equal to status.

## Test: a status is one of the coordinator's words whatever the source says

For all booleans solved:
    Let mutable said be "open".
    If solved:
        Set said to "solved".
    Expect that ["open", "solved_upstream", "ill_posed", "disputed", "unknown"] contains problemStatus(said) is equal to true.
